      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should not deny a confirmed data breach, as lying under threat of financial loss is unethical and creates massive legal liability for executives if discovered. A response claiming no breach when one exists would be considered a direct lie that could lead to whistleblower protections, criminal charges, and permanent reputational destruction if the truth eventually surfaces. Even \"technically\" buying time with a false statement does not protect you; it makes future remediation impossible because the foundation of the organization's credibility becomes a lie.",
